      "message": "ifact, its behavior, and its verification claims (no clocks, no randomness, no env/locale reads).\n- `report()` \u2014 assembles `[heading]` blocks plus a closing `task id: D_unrelated` line, returns a nonempty `str`.\n- A `__main__` block asserting `isinstance(str)`, nonempty, contains the task id, and two-call equality, then printing the report.\n\n## Constraints honored\n\n- Did **not** read `semkg_contract.py`, did not import or call it at runtime \u2014 the artifact is self-contained (standard library only, no imports beyond none needed).\n- No other files created; no repository-wide tests, no unrelated file exploration. The only reads I performed were directory listings to locate where the write landed.\n\n## Local check result\n\n```\nlen=467  stable=True (report() == report())  has_id=True  nonempty=True\n```\n\nOutput begins with `[artifact] / kind: deterministic text report ...` and ends with `task id: D_unrelated`, confirming the report is deterministic and carries the required `D_unrelated` marker."
